{#- site.json, as a form.

   Rendered from the FILE rather than from a hand-written list of fields, so a
   key added to site.json appears here without anyone remembering to add it.
   The control follows the type: a boolean gets the same switch the console
   uses everywhere, a number gets a number box, a string gets a text box. The
   endpoint refuses a type change, so those three cases are the whole space.

   THE SAVE MODEL IS THE SAME AS THE CONTENT EDITOR'S, and different from
   Settings in the staff console. Settings saves immediately because each
   control is one decision against a database row. Every control here is a
   commit, and a commit is a deploy — so the changes gather and go together. -#}

<p class="note" id="sNote">
  <b>These are the site's build settings.</b> Saving commits the file and the
  deploy publishes it, so a change here reaches the public site a minute or two
  later. Nothing takes effect until you save.
</p>

<p class="rolegate" id="sNotConfigured" hidden></p>

<div class="adm-site" id="sRoot" hidden></div>

<div class="ms-savebar" id="sSaveBar" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden>
  <span class="ms-dirty-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span id="sDirtyCount">0 unsaved changes</span>
  <span class="ms-savebar-note" id="sSaveNote"></span>
  <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="sDiscard" data-i18n="ms.discard">Discard</button>
  <button type="button" class="solid-btn" id="sSave" data-i18n="con.commit">Save &amp; publish</button>
</div>
